AI Brief — Friday, 13 November 2026 (IST) — last 24 hours

> Jensen Huang has resigned as Nvidia CEO, with CFO Colette Kress stepping in, and nonprofits have sued five AI labs to freeze frontier models.
> Google shipped Gemini 4 Hydrogen, SpaceX plans $74 billion in AI campuses, and India's IT ministry is questioning how gig-worker video is used to train robots.

# WORLD

No confirmed military AI incident (an attack or accident involving AI) in this window. The main defence story is a report on Britain's plans for AI targeting.

### Report: UK defence ministry wants targeting that is "autonomous by default"
The Bureau of Investigative Journalism says official documents it obtained describe a Ministry of Defence targeting system that is "autonomous by default, human by exception", with a first version of its Digital Targeting Web expected next year. That would be a sharp change from the UK's earlier stress on human control. This is based on the Bureau's reading of the documents and has not been confirmed by the ministry. It lands days before UN talks on autonomous weapons in Geneva from 16 to 20 November. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)
Source: The Bureau of Investigative Journalism https://www.thebureauinvestigates.com/stories/2026-11-13/revealed-mod-aiming-to-remove-humans-from-military-targeting-decisions

# USA

### Jensen Huang resigns as Nvidia CEO; Colette Kress named interim chief
Huang stepped down on Thursday, US time, after reports of extramarital affairs, including one with a woman US intelligence officials reportedly believe was recruited by Chinese intelligence. He also leaves the board. CFO Colette Kress is interim CEO while the board searches inside and outside the company, and longtime director Harvey Jones becomes Nvidia's first board chair. Reuters says the shares closed down 4.3%. China has called the spying allegations baseless, and Nvidia still plans to report earnings next week. (Theme: AI industry and startup news)
Source: NPR https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/nx-s1-6037833/jensen-huang-nvidia-board-fired
Also: The Japan Times https://www.japantimes.co.jp/business/2026/11/13/companies/nvidia-huang-ousted/

### Nonprofits sue five AI labs to freeze more capable models
A coalition of safety and consumer groups filed suit in San Francisco Superior Court against Anthropic, Google, Meta, OpenAI and SpaceXSI. They are asking the court to halt training and release of models more capable than today's, and they point to the companies' own warnings about bioweapon and cyberattack risks. These are the plaintiffs' claims. No court has ruled yet. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)
Source: Al Jazeera https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/12/us-nonprofits-sue-tech-giants-to-halt-ai-development

### Google launches Gemini 4 Hydrogen, a fast model for coding and agents
Google says Hydrogen brings near-frontier intelligence at lower cost and higher speed. It is rolling out across the Gemini API, AI Studio, Search, the Gemini app and its Antigravity coding tool. Speed and quality claims come from Google. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: Google https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-hydrogen/

### SpaceX plans more than $74 billion in AI supercomputing campuses
SpaceX says it will build two AI computing sites: about $50 billion in Arizona and up to $24 billion in Texas near Starbase, where the facility will generate its own power. The Arizona site still needs local approval. It shows how compute and power are becoming the main AI build-out story. (Theme: Technology trends)
Source: The Hill https://thehill.com/policy/technology/6217630-spacex-plans-data-centers-texas-arizona/

# CHINA

### Tencent launches Hy Realtime, a voice model that can sing and use tools
Tencent's Hunyuan team released Hy Realtime, a real-time voice model that recovers meaning from half-finished or self-corrected speech, decides on its own when to search the web, and can sing songs on request. It is live in Yuanbao voice calls and Tencent customer service, and a Tencent Cloud API is coming. Its quality claims come from Tencent's own tests. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: IT Home (Chinese) https://www.ithome.com/1/026/825.htm

### China Telecom releases a model trained entirely on Huawei Ascend chips
Xing4.0-29B-A4B is a mixture-of-experts model with 29 billion parameters, of which 4 billion are active at a time. China Telecom says it is the first model of its size trained fully on Ascend NPUs with the MindSpore framework, and it reports a SWE-bench Verified score of 75.0. Those are developer figures, but the release is a real test of China's push to train models without Nvidia. (Theme: AI breakthroughs)
Source: TheNextGenTechInsider https://www.thenextgentechinsider.com/pulse/china-telecom-launches-xing40-29b-a4b-mixture-of-experts-model

# ASIA

### Japan to launch an AI safety partnership with ASEAN
Digital Minister Toshiharu Furukawa said Japan will start an AI safety and security partnership with the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), citing the misuse of AI in cyberattacks. Details have not been released yet. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)
Source: Nikkei (Japanese) https://www.nikkei.com/article/DGXZQOUA1319C0T11C26A1000000/

### Korea Aerospace tests AI drone navigation that works without GPS
At a defence AI summit in Seoul, KAI said it is flight-testing AI that lets drones fix their own position when GPS is jammed. It is also developing an AI pilot, KAiLOT, with Konan Technology so drones can fly alongside FA-50 jets. These are company statements on work in progress. (Theme: Technology trends)
Source: Edaily https://en.edaily.co.kr/news/eda202611135302/

# INDIA

### MeitY questions platforms that film homes to train robots
The IT ministry met Snabbit, Pronto, Urban Company and robotics firms on Thursday about gig workers wearing head cameras to record household tasks for physical-AI training, ET reports, citing three people. Officials asked about consent, privacy and data-storage safeguards. Pronto has started in-home recording, while Urban Company and Snabbit decided against it. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)
Source: The Economic Times https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/newsletters/morning-dispatch/meity-flags-physical-ai-data-use-us-data-centre-woes-may-benefit-india/articleshow/135786144.cms

### CAG to unveil an in-house audit LLM built by IIT Madras
The Comptroller and Auditor General will launch CAG LLM 2.0, trained on about 65,000 internal inspection reports. It will help auditors with groundwork and analysis but will not carry out audits on its own. The launch is set for Audit Diwas on 16 November. (Theme: AI industry and startup news)
Source: Rediff https://www.rediff.com/business/report/cag-to-launch-in-house-llm-20-developed-by-iit-madras-for-enhanced-auditing/20261113.htm
Also: Business Standard https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/cag-to-launch-in-house-ai-model-to-help-auditors-analyse-financial-data-126111201735_1.html

### NTT DATA and IIT Jammu set up an AI centre for climate resilience
The new centre will apply AI, digital twins and sensors to floods and landslides in the Tawi and Chenab river basins, and will include research on Dogri-language AI and a startup lab. (Theme: Technology trends)
Source: Express Computer https://www.expresscomputer.in/amp/news/ntt-data-and-iit-jammu-to-establish-ai-coe-focused-on-climate-resilience/141307/

